SEVERITY: wrong -- every popup:= opens the last form written, and the run can crash.

popupAttrBindsAction -- popup:=aForm binds to utilities' own popup action when Utilities is on the search list while the
form is defined. One name, one field: each popup:= re-points that one field, so every popup then opens the LAST form
written. Found 2026-11-25 (kant, SEQ 777) preparing the watched run in IncantForms/WorkingOn/tester: with colorList shown
after, every popup:= opened colorWords and the run died at exit 139.
The same family as seal 527's finding: a name on the search list is reopened by a define under another registry.

WORKAROUND: define the forms first, search Utilities after (tester does). A form file read under show is not affected:
Utilities is not searched at its define.

